               gettext,
               python3
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: flickos-kits
Architecture: all
# python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0: the window, GTK 3 so it follows the Arc theme.
# flickos-software 1.20: the kits are apps in its catalog (Developer Tools), and
# it installs and removes them, with the plan first. The terminal for the SSH
# key and Rust (xdg-terminal-exec) and wl-copy for the public key are left out
# of the window when missing, so neither is a dependency.
Depends: python3,
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         flickos-software (>= 1.21),
         ${misc:Depends}
# Its rows run settings that only these versions have: flickos-control's
# packet-capture, wireless.test-adapter and upstream.ID (1.84), and
# Software's Security Tools for the security kits (1.24). A test version
# says so with Breaks (docs/05-apt-repository.md, "Testing packages"); at
# release they become Depends with the plain numbers.
Breaks: flickos-control (<< 1.84~),
        flickos-software (<< 1.24~)
Description: install and set up the FlickOS developer and security kits
 A small window, Tool Kits, to install the kit for each kind of work (Python,
 Node.js, C and C++, containers, and security work such as network analysis
 or forensics) with a switch, and to set up what an installed kit needs:
 git's name and email, an SSH key, Rust, capturing packets without
 administrator rights, a Wi-Fi adapter for testing. Installing and removing
 go through Software, with the plan shown first.
 .
 Nothing is installed by default and nothing runs in the background. The
 setup steps change your own files only through the programs that own them
 (git, ssh-keygen, rustup), and only when you press their button; the ones
 that change the computer are settings of FlickOS's Settings, which asks for
 the administrator's password and keeps them in History.
